      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding is that registerDefaultNetworkCallback (which Setting and SUW can use) won\u0027t report the true default network if there\u0027s a VPN active, but registerSystemDefaultNetworkCallback (which SUW *cannot* use) does give the underlying default network.\n\nThe default network status is used to control\n1) \"!\" icon in the Wifi pie (if wifi isn\u0027t default)\n2) \"Low quality\" summary if wifi is connected but cell is default (due to the wifi score being low).\n3) Letting Settings know if carrier merged wifi is default or not (to show \"W+\" instead of LTE/5G) (not a SUW case)",
